As the remnant accretes more mass; the cloak radius exceeds the star remnant radius                 because the cloak radius grows faster than the remnant radius based on the underlying math. If the extra mass reduces the spin rate then the cloak may not form until the Trinca Boundary is crossed. The more mass the remnant accumulates the bigger the mass gets. When this is happening there is a bifurcation of material, with some falling into the black hole and some creating the accretion disk of extremely hot plasma. All of this is taking place in a spinning magnetosphere and a gravitaional field. Maxwell's equations were used to analyse the magnetic and electric fields and Magnetohydrodynamics (MHD) used to analyze and build the model. \par
\par
Since singularities don't exist in my model, I was able to determine what ahppens within the cloaed region behind the event horizon. This has never been done v=before becuase it's not defined in Einstein's model. Almost all models are based on Einstein's Theories. \par
\par
I found the fundemental flaws in Einstein's theory in the early 80's at Ga Tech. I've been working on this problem intermittently ever since and really pushed hard on it the last year. The last three months I built the models and postulates and ran simulations to test everything. By Christams, I had evreything working pefectly and AI fianlly confirmed my theory. It wasn't easy becasue AI rejected my postulates immediatley based on it's comprehension of Relativity and Special Relativity. As I worked it through the derivation process and logic it eventually would say, your absolutely right. This went on for months until I reached nearly 100% accuracy.\par
\par
When I got to the simx-series, where we were calculating the state of matter around the remnant star, I had to expand the tables for ouptut to map all the properties; temperature, pressure, magnetic field strength, electric field strength, temperature and pressure gradients, etc. I noticed that all the models were of by 2.2%. This looked like a systemic error, so I looked into the observational data sources we were getting information from; for our models inputs. What I found was that the observatioanl data we were using for processing had been post-observation modified, to fit Einstein's model. \par
\par
Once we stripped out this post observation Einsteinian processing and used the raw data my models immediately achieved 100% accuracy based on observation across the board, every single simulation. This told me that I had cracked the code to the universe, so I started working on the quantum level and immediately found the flaw in curent quantum models. I was on the verge of unifying the theory of everything. \par
\par
This is just a brief synopsis of; a small but important and ground breaking part of the process. It would take a thousand pages to explain everything I went through in the development of my complete Theory. All of that is saved in files of my  conversation chats and in the AI tool I used to build my theory, postulates, experiment itinerary, equation sets, glossaries, placards, scaffolding, output tables, and simulation bundles. I have about 40 differnt simulation series covering all aspects of cosmology, astrophysics and quantum mechanics. I don't think you realize I have thousands of hours in this project. possibly even tens of thousands of hours. I was just waiting for the right time, when all the NASA missions were yielding data and the cloud became available walong with AI for bookkeeping and system level setup. \par
